WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:05.885
One year ago, we arrived on a piece of land
we just bought in Portugal.

00:00:06.171 --> 00:00:09.364
We came with one van, on a big piece of land.

00:00:09.626 --> 00:00:11.653
With a lot of rain falling, like a lot.

00:00:11.653 --> 00:00:14.624
It rains more here than in London, or The Netherlands.

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.199
It was raining all day...

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:18.209
And I wasn't really prepared for that...

00:00:18.209 --> 00:00:20.159
I mean: it's Portugal, should be sunny...

00:00:20.792 --> 00:00:26.161
So, it meant daily wet socks,
and trying to dry stuff, in a very humid van.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:29.836
There wasn't much here...

00:00:29.836 --> 00:00:31.676
We got water from a local tap.

00:00:31.676 --> 00:00:33.377
And, this was the toilet...

00:00:33.892 --> 00:00:35.532
That's a poop hole.

00:00:35.532 --> 00:00:38.231
And, the goal for this year, was to set up a Basekamp.

00:00:38.672 --> 00:00:42.483
Set up some basic infrastructure, so we can be here with more people.

00:00:42.483 --> 00:00:44.969
So, here we have our first Kamp-fire...

00:00:44.969 --> 00:00:46.945
Get it? Kamp-fire?

00:00:46.945 --> 00:00:48.238
Uh, yeah, good joke...

00:00:48.238 --> 00:00:53.452
Anyway, there was a lot of work to do,
and this video has all the progress we made in one year.

00:00:56.206 --> 00:00:57.281
So, the land is big.

00:00:57.281 --> 00:00:58.491
It's 10 hectares.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:01.188
And, at this point, we haven't really seen the entire land.

00:01:01.188 --> 00:01:04.783
Only with a drone, because it's really hard to access everything.

00:01:04.783 --> 00:01:07.160
Fully overgrown, with thorns.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.123
So, we started making pathways.

00:01:09.123 --> 00:01:12.149
So, we need to go through the bushes, somewhere here...

00:02:00.318 --> 00:02:03.613
So, we made a path all around the land,
and we could walk around much better.

00:02:03.613 --> 00:02:07.420
Wait, let me actually give you a better perspective
of the land, to keep an overview...

00:02:08.107 --> 00:02:12.592
So, we go here, the land is here,
and this is the path we just made.

00:02:13.107 --> 00:02:14.800
Let's keep a list of all the things we did.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.410
Make pathways: check!

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:19.526
And, as a reference, here's the highest point on the land.

00:02:19.526 --> 00:02:20.588
It has a big rock.

00:02:21.078 --> 00:02:23.649
This is what the view looks like from here.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:33.351
Now, with pathways, we can explore much more,
and doing so, we started seeing some things.

00:02:33.743 --> 00:02:36.236
Like, over here, we saw a puddle of water.

00:02:36.359 --> 00:02:40.024
We got curious to how big it was, so we cleared up the space around it.

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:45.068
We removed a lot of spiky bushes,
and chopped down a bunch of dead trees.

00:02:48.263 --> 00:02:51.609
And, while doing all of this, we also found
a few random things in there...

00:02:52.001 --> 00:02:53.046
Wow!

00:02:53.831 --> 00:02:55.504
A cow bone!

00:02:55.504 --> 00:02:57.417
What's happening in this part?

00:02:57.417 --> 00:03:00.230
- Looks like burnt plastic...

00:03:00.769 --> 00:03:04.259
Also found some more stuff, like this metal...

00:03:04.259 --> 00:03:05.520
From a motorbike...

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:09.430
So, now, it's ready.

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:14.175
Okay, it still looks a bit rough, but this little swamp
could potentially be a place to swim, in the future.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:19.529
And, just for your reference, this little swamp 
is located right here on the map.

00:03:19.529 --> 00:03:24.196
But, from some neighbors, we actually hear there should be
a bigger water source on the land, right there.

00:03:24.822 --> 00:03:28.509
Looking from above, it should be
somewhere hidden, between these bushes?

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:34.710
It's hard to imagine, but when we walked down,
we noticed it does look like something is there.

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:37.106
Underneath these dead trees.

00:03:37.253 --> 00:03:39.981
So, we started to drag them out, and clear it up.

00:03:43.597 --> 00:03:44.978
Mattia took a little dip.

00:03:44.978 --> 00:03:46.451
First swim of the year.

00:03:47.054 --> 00:03:48.444
22nd of February.

00:03:48.959 --> 00:03:50.337
Be nice and lovely...

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:55.765
And, it turned out to be quite a big reservoir of water.

00:03:56.255 --> 00:03:57.250
Before...

00:03:57.809 --> 00:03:58.467
After!

00:03:58.709 --> 00:04:00.420
And, all of this work is quite fun.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:02.370
Discovering these new things on the land.

00:04:02.713 --> 00:04:07.066
But, it's also intense, because at this point,
we have very basic tools.

00:04:07.066 --> 00:04:09.527
We really needed to start setting up our Basekamp.

00:04:10.312 --> 00:04:14.875
So, a few months ago, before we came to the land,
we got two old shipping containers.

00:04:15.194 --> 00:04:17.444
We needed them to move our stuff to the land.

00:04:17.444 --> 00:04:21.992
But, we figured: if we move a container anyway,
let's also turn them into something useful.

00:04:21.992 --> 00:04:23.870
Not just a box to ship things...

00:04:24.655 --> 00:04:29.023
So, we converted one container in
a fully equipped workspace, with all our tools.

00:04:29.489 --> 00:04:33.324
And, the other one, we call the Town Center,
and it has all the basic utilities.

00:04:33.324 --> 00:04:37.134
Like, a kitchen, fridge, washing machine, things like that.

00:04:37.747 --> 00:04:40.614
So, once we've built them, 
we packed them up, and send them off.

00:04:46.797 --> 00:04:49.711
They came to Portugal, with some very sketch unloading.

00:04:49.711 --> 00:04:51.718
Kind of a scary moment.

00:04:51.718 --> 00:04:53.430
It felt like they could fall at any point.

00:04:53.773 --> 00:04:58.832
I mean, it's a fully packed shipping container,
on two individual forklifts, and a muddy road.

00:04:59.834 --> 00:05:01.711
But, at this moment, they're not on the land yet.

00:05:01.711 --> 00:05:03.516
Just in a storage place close by.

00:05:03.516 --> 00:05:07.078
Because, before they could come,
we still have to make some space.

00:05:08.206 --> 00:05:11.137
So, we currently have the Basekamp
 installed on this grass patch.

00:05:11.137 --> 00:05:13.420
Where we have the two shipping containers coming.

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:17.460
So, I want to clear up the bushes and thorns here,
 a little bit until the trees.

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:20.937
So, the containers can go there, and we have a bit more space.

00:05:24.664 --> 00:05:29.704
Which means, yeah, taking down a few more
spiky bushes and leveling the floor.

00:05:29.704 --> 00:05:32.201
To make sure the containers are parked flat.

00:05:33.035 --> 00:05:34.677
So, finally, they got dropped off on the land.

00:05:34.677 --> 00:05:36.402
Luckily, everything went okay.

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:37.962
They arrived in one piece.

00:05:37.962 --> 00:05:41.027
And, first, they dropped the workspace, and then the kitchen.

00:05:41.689 --> 00:05:43.112
This was a big upgrade!

00:05:43.112 --> 00:05:46.008
We suddenly have a lot of tools, and a place to be dry.

00:05:46.572 --> 00:05:48.247
We call this Basekamp.

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:52.415
This is the main place, where we'll camp out
in the coming years, as we work on the land.

00:05:52.415 --> 00:05:54.950
So, we figured let's make it nice around here.

00:05:56.470 --> 00:05:58.702
We started cleaning up the area around it.

00:05:58.702 --> 00:06:04.025
Remove some spiky bushes, level the soil,
and plant a herbal garden with some flowers.

00:06:26.531 --> 00:06:30.764
At this point, the place looks nice,
and we have this fully equipped kitchen, and workspace.

00:06:31.156 --> 00:06:34.605
However, there's no electricity yet, so we can't use anything.

00:06:35.758 --> 00:06:38.931
So, we made a big metal frame to mount on top of the container...

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:41.571
We installed the solar panels on the roof...

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:46.483
Installed all the components for our solar system,
and connected all the cables.

00:06:46.875 --> 00:06:49.149
Okay: moment of truth, everything is wired up...

00:06:49.149 --> 00:06:50.969
Solar panels coming in here...

00:06:50.969 --> 00:06:57.542
The only thing breaking the circuit is the fuse box,
 so if we put this one on, everything should work.

00:06:57.542 --> 00:06:59.137
So, let's see...

00:07:04.336 --> 00:07:05.638
That seems to work...

00:07:05.638 --> 00:07:07.639
To be honest, this was quite a magical moment.

00:07:07.639 --> 00:07:10.999
Suddenly, we could use everything, like the blender.

00:07:13.893 --> 00:07:17.297
But, besides electricity, we needed another crucial thing: water.

00:07:18.744 --> 00:07:22.840
Because, up until this point, all the water
we use still comes from our jerrycans.

00:07:23.276 --> 00:07:26.185
We refill them in a village nearby, and bring them to the land.

00:07:26.734 --> 00:07:30.390
But, actually, the upside of all the rain,
is that there's plenty of water around us.

00:07:30.390 --> 00:07:34.647
So, we found an old abandoned well on a spring,
on the land of the neighbors.

00:07:35.334 --> 00:07:36.916
The spring is right here.

00:07:36.916 --> 00:07:40.959
And, they turned it into a well, but it's abandoned,
 and not used for many years.

00:07:40.959 --> 00:07:45.472
So, we asked the neighbor, if we could 
use his well, and clean it up.

00:07:45.472 --> 00:07:46.573
And, he said yes.

00:07:46.916 --> 00:07:49.594
So, we cleaned up the area around it, and opened it up.

00:07:49.913 --> 00:07:51.614
It looks impressive.

00:07:54.344 --> 00:07:56.062
But, first, a little swim, you know?

00:07:56.062 --> 00:07:57.521
Quality control.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.217
Yeah, maybe not the best for drinking...

00:08:04.775 --> 00:08:06.903
So, we asked some guys to help out cleaning it.

00:08:06.903 --> 00:08:09.399
Rita asked them to mount a GoPro on their head.

00:08:09.938 --> 00:08:12.275
So, they got in there, and emptied the well.

00:08:12.275 --> 00:08:14.034
We got some funny footage from that...

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:25.536
And, once it was done, we started digging the pipes in the ground.

00:08:25.536 --> 00:08:30.739
We connected all the tubes above the ground,
and we assembled all the parts for the water system.

00:08:30.739 --> 00:08:32.335
Which, is using a pressure tank.

00:08:32.703 --> 00:08:34.089
And, we installed everything.

00:08:40.308 --> 00:08:41.977
So, Rita, can you show the water?

00:08:41.977 --> 00:08:43.363
- Yes! The water!

00:08:43.363 --> 00:08:44.572
Look at this!

00:08:45.766 --> 00:08:46.677
Water...

00:08:47.462 --> 00:08:48.534
Water...

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:49.850
Water...

00:08:51.419 --> 00:08:52.281
- It's cold!

00:08:54.537 --> 00:08:56.558
And finally, also, a shower.

00:08:56.754 --> 00:08:58.331
Well, sort of...

00:08:58.699 --> 00:09:01.227
A few weeks later, we upgraded to a decent shower.

00:09:02.846 --> 00:09:04.956
So, we now have hot showers...

00:09:05.814 --> 00:09:08.022
Yeah! This is good!

00:09:11.112 --> 00:09:14.476
So now, we have local water powered on solar energy.

00:09:14.844 --> 00:09:18.655
But, one thing missing after six months:
an upgrade to the poop hole.

00:09:19.194 --> 00:09:21.357
It got kind of essential, at this point.

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:24.730
So, Ian came, and he built a nice little compost toilet.

00:09:27.525 --> 00:09:29.385
With a seat from recycled plastic.

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:33.000
Works with sawdust, and you add a scoop after you poop.

00:09:35.845 --> 00:09:40.095
So, at this moment, we have water, electricity,
a dry space, and a shower.

00:09:40.095 --> 00:09:44.730
It's quite a proper Basekamp with good utilities,
and it's set up right there.

00:09:45.122 --> 00:09:47.553
So, now it's time to work a bit more on the land.

00:09:48.632 --> 00:09:50.133
Now, it's getting pretty hot in summer.

00:09:50.133 --> 00:09:54.114
But, we have a little stream on the land,
but it's covered again with bushes.

00:09:55.046 --> 00:09:57.506
So, our moms came to help out, and clean it up.

00:10:01.465 --> 00:10:05.464
Take away dead trees, and thorns,
so we can access the fresh, flowing water.

00:10:07.573 --> 00:10:10.641
Now, we have a nice place to swim, and refresh.

00:10:13.461 --> 00:10:15.991
We also build a little dam, from the rocks.

00:10:15.991 --> 00:10:18.222
And, the water rises, so we can take a dip.

00:10:19.546 --> 00:10:22.969
And this stream we cleared, is located right there,
at the edge of the land.

00:10:23.705 --> 00:10:28.202
But, what we actually really wanted to clear up,
was a little ruin located here on the land.

00:10:29.054 --> 00:10:31.910
It's a small building, built on a granite foundation.

00:10:32.106 --> 00:10:34.421
And apparently, it was a kitchen in the old days.

00:10:34.862 --> 00:10:37.356
Also fully overgrown, and hard to access.

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:42.177
We chopped down the overgrowing thorns,
so we could go around it.

00:10:42.643 --> 00:10:45.825
Cleared the inside, which was, for some reason, full of soil.

00:10:48.792 --> 00:10:51.491
And, we took down the almost collapsing roof...

00:10:54.707 --> 00:10:57.592
It was really nice, to finally be able to access this building.

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:01.215
And, it has quite a beautiful location,
with a view on the field.

00:11:02.665 --> 00:11:05.904
Now, we have one more ruin to clean,
and this one scared us actually a bit...

00:11:05.904 --> 00:11:10.108
Because, it's way, way bigger, and way more overgrown...

00:11:11.663 --> 00:11:16.489
It's hidden here, between the bushes,
so we invited some friends, to help us clear it.

00:11:50.742 --> 00:11:55.587
And, after a few days, we managed to take out all the spiky bushes,
and trees that are grown into it.

00:11:56.225 --> 00:11:59.195
Now, we can take measurements,
and make a plan on what to do with it.

00:11:59.391 --> 00:12:01.109
You will see more of that in Season 2.

00:12:01.747 --> 00:12:04.162
And, here you can see how they are positioned on the land.

00:12:04.554 --> 00:12:06.931
Big ruin, small ruin, Basekamp.

00:12:07.936 --> 00:12:10.647
So, as you might have guessed, it's right there on the map.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:14.951
And, by now, we actually became quite
good friends with the neighbors.

00:12:14.951 --> 00:12:17.983
They're always driving with their tractors,
seeing what's going on.

00:12:18.964 --> 00:12:22.564
Most of them are above sixty,
and they grew up around this land.

00:12:22.564 --> 00:12:24.189
They know it inside out...

00:12:25.023 --> 00:12:27.398
I don't think they really understand what we're doing...

00:12:27.398 --> 00:12:30.348
I mean, we're not even really sure, but they like it.

00:12:32.292 --> 00:12:35.748
And, they might be older, but they're still very active,
and happy to help out.

00:12:35.881 --> 00:12:40.046
Using their tractors, to connect a wood chipper,
and chip some trees.

00:12:40.046 --> 00:12:41.800
Or, help us to move big stuff.

00:12:42.462 --> 00:12:45.440
And, they also often bring us food,
which they grow on their own land.

00:12:45.906 --> 00:12:47.616
Potatoes...

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:51.967
Fernanda.

00:12:52.459 --> 00:12:55.598
The neighbor?
- The neighbors!

00:12:57.250 --> 00:12:59.274
Look at this!

00:12:59.274 --> 00:13:00.200
It's really nice.

00:13:00.592 --> 00:13:04.743
And, in exchange, we help them a bit harvesting,
things like potatoes.

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:07.781
Or, grapes for their wine.

00:13:09.731 --> 00:13:13.968
And, besides making friend with neighbors,
we also observed a lot of friends around.

00:13:14.262 --> 00:13:16.545
Little birds, that eat our leftover bread...

00:13:17.182 --> 00:13:19.772
Caterpillars, that are walking around through our pathways...

00:13:20.625 --> 00:13:24.393
Or, slowly eating our plants, bit by bit...

00:13:24.959 --> 00:13:26.451
Frogs from the swamp...

00:13:26.846 --> 00:13:29.636
Goats and sheep from the neighbors, that eat our grass...

00:13:29.636 --> 00:13:31.973
And, probably, this is the friendliest friend...

00:13:31.973 --> 00:13:34.576
We have a guest for dinner tonight.

00:13:43.060 --> 00:13:45.280
Yeah, they always drop by, to see what's going on...

00:13:45.476 --> 00:13:47.222
We have very welcoming friends.

00:13:48.644 --> 00:13:51.294
So, towards the end of the year, winter is approaching.

00:13:51.686 --> 00:13:53.673
It's getting colder, and the days are shorter.

00:13:54.212 --> 00:13:55.833
We noticed something missing...

00:13:55.833 --> 00:14:00.219
Up until now, everything was very practical,
like getting water, electricity, a toilet...

00:14:00.735 --> 00:14:03.477
We needed a fun social activity in our routine.

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:05.862
So, we made a pizza oven, from clay.

00:14:06.209 --> 00:14:09.882
And another essential thing needed for it,
was a roof to keep it dry.

00:14:10.345 --> 00:14:11.468
Because, yeah, remember?

00:14:11.468 --> 00:14:14.486
More rains here than The Netherlands, or I guess Italy...

00:14:15.369 --> 00:14:16.917
So, we gathered some materials...

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:22.293
And, we used some roof tiles,
from the big ruin, we just cleaned up.

00:14:22.759 --> 00:14:24.499
And, we built a wooden structure with it.

00:14:30.304 --> 00:14:32.708
A roof to protect from the rain in the winter.

00:14:34.375 --> 00:14:38.380
So, now we can just work outside,
when it rains, without getting wet.

00:14:38.718 --> 00:14:44.322
Which, is a big upgrade, but more importantly,
we can bake pizza all year round.

00:14:47.635 --> 00:14:51.114
So, it's now raining, but we eat pizza dry.

00:14:52.385 --> 00:14:55.209
Now, this is our saturday routine: big delicious pizzas.

00:14:57.009 --> 00:15:00.000
And, the pizza oven is set up right here,
in the middle of Basekamp.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:03.894
So, we can eat as much as possible:
breakfast, lunch, dinner, midnight snack...

00:15:04.409 --> 00:15:06.534
And finally, a last build of the year.

00:15:06.534 --> 00:15:08.618
A roof in front of the Town Center.

00:15:09.329 --> 00:15:11.724
Because, every time it rains, it gets all muddy inside...

00:15:12.141 --> 00:15:14.118
When the sun shines, it gets very hot...

00:15:14.314 --> 00:15:19.438
So, we made a wooden structure, with an experimental roof,
mad from recycled plastic sheets.

00:15:28.735 --> 00:15:30.888
It's a bit of a living prototype...

00:15:31.158 --> 00:15:33.386
We're not sure how it's gonna go, but let's see.

00:15:38.154 --> 00:15:42.086
All right, so that was Season 1,
compressed into a short video.

00:15:42.650 --> 00:15:44.966
It was quite an intense year, I would say...

00:15:44.966 --> 00:15:46.763
A lot of things to do...

00:15:46.763 --> 00:15:49.614
It was very raw, when we first came on the land.

00:15:49.614 --> 00:15:51.493
All the rain, and just the van...

00:15:52.572 --> 00:15:57.808
But, there's something very satisfying, about really starting basic,
and see small upgrades.

00:15:58.225 --> 00:16:02.385
Like, the first time we had a cutter for the bushes,
or having electricity, or water.

00:16:02.728 --> 00:16:08.394
Really makes you appreciate these basic things, 
which is really nice to be a part of that.

00:16:08.762 --> 00:16:11.291
And, the goal of this year, was to set up a Basekamp.

00:16:11.291 --> 00:16:16.278
To have a place, where we can be with more people, 
and set up some basic infrastructure.

00:16:16.768 --> 00:16:19.491
So, it was mainly me, and Rita, here on the land.

00:16:19.957 --> 00:16:22.629
And, some friends and family came to help, here and there.

00:16:23.022 --> 00:16:28.427
And, throughout time, towards the end of the year,
Adrian and Julie came to help out, for longer periods of time.

00:16:28.868 --> 00:16:32.116
But, the goal is really to not do 
too much on the land itself.

00:16:32.508 --> 00:16:35.210
And because, we first wanted to see where we even are...

00:16:35.602 --> 00:16:36.998
What does the land need?

00:16:36.998 --> 00:16:41.052
What is the plan we're going to do, 
before we start chopping down, and intervening too much?

00:16:41.690 --> 00:16:46.003
So, the goal was to set up a Basekamp, 
so we can invite more people, to come and help out.

00:16:46.003 --> 00:16:47.688
And, meanwhile think of a good plan...

00:16:47.835 --> 00:16:48.786
And we've been doing that.

00:16:48.786 --> 00:16:49.928
We have a Basekamp now.

00:16:49.928 --> 00:16:53.280
We thought of a good plan, and that's 
what we're going to do in Season 2.

00:16:53.623 --> 00:16:57.335
